  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PreRC 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'As preclinical research gets underway, scientists must follow safety
    guidelines and obtain approvals before lab and animal studies can continue. You
    help organize paperwork, track approvals, and confirm that the research follows
    ethical standards.


    <b>As the research coordinator, what is your role in
    this situation?</b>'
  explanation: "During preclinical research, research coordinators help make sure
    studies are done safely and ethically by organizing important paperwork, tracking
    required approvals, and confirming that research teams follow established guidelines.
    While research coordinators aren\u2019t responsible for approving studies or
    running experiments, they help keep everything organized and on track behind
    the scenes."
  correctAnswer: Making sure the research has the right approvals and follows safety
    and ethical guidelines
  incorrectAnswer1: Reviewing the research and determining whether it meets ethical
    standards
  incorrectAnswer2: Designing safety experiments to test whether the new treatment
    is ready to be tested in people
  incorrectAnswer3: Deciding when the research is ready to move forward into clinical
    trials
  questionRole: Research Coordinator
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: PreClinical
